 3. 🇷🇺 Trump&#x27;s diesel deal 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump announced yesterday that he's reached a deal with Russia to increase the supply of diesel to the U.S. and global markets.

 The announcement came as U.S. diesel prices hovered near record highs and Ukrainian and European diplomats arrived in Miami for talks on ending the war with Russia. 📞 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told Axios' Barak Ravid in a phone interview yesterday that Trump's decision to unilaterally lift sanctions on Russia and allow it to export diesel was "not fair and not honest."

 Trump's announcement, which came after a call with Russian President Vladimir Putin, shocked Ukraine and many European governments and created a new crisis between the U.S. and its Western allies. "You know, it looks like a happy birthday present for Putin. It looks absolutely terrible," Zelensky said in frustration, referring to the Russian president's birthday earlier this week. The other side: Trump decided to strike a deal with Russia after Zelensky ignored half a dozen U.S. requests to stop attacking Russian oil refineries, a U.S. official with direct knowledge told Axios' Barak Ravid.

 "Zelensky is misreading the room. By continuing to hit refineries, he is eroding the goodwill that he has built with Trump over the last six months," the U.S. official said. Go deeper . 

 
 
