 4. ✈️ Chart du jour: Fuel squeeze 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Energy Information Administration. Chart: Matt Phillips/Axios Soaring jet fuel prices — driven up by the Iran war — have been pushing airfares higher and prompting airlines to cut flights, Axios' Pete Gannon reports. 

 Case in point: Delta Air Lines said yesterday its fuel bill will be $6 billion higher this year, a 60% jump from last year. Zoom out: U.S. airfares were up 23.4% in August from a year earlier, according to the latest federal inflation data, with airlines passing rising fuel costs along to travelers.

 Travelers are also seeing fewer flight options, as carriers have cut unprofitable flights. Share this story . 

 
 
