 7. 🐻 Remembering fiery Mike Ditka 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chicago Bears coach Mike Ditka yells at quarterback Jim Harbaugh during a game against the San Francisco 49ers on Dec. 14, 1987. Photo: Ed Wagner/Chicago Tribune via Getty Images Mike Ditka, who died yesterday at 86, was "Iron Mike" as a player who revolutionized the tight end position. He became easily recognizable, and often imitated, as the bellowing, mustachioed, sweater-vest-wearing "Da Coach" of the Chicago Bears during a Super Bowl-winning tenure.

 Former President Obama wrote on X : "When I got to Chicago in the summer of 1985, Mike Ditka and the Chicago Bears were king. Coach Ditka set the tone for a team that was punishing, dominant, and fun — and the city loved him for it. I'm thinking of the Ditka family and Bears fans everywhere on the passing of a legend." NYT obit (gift link). 

 
 
